NeoPulse is an independent implementation, but parts of its design derive from
SidePulse by Peter Kuhar (https://sidepulse.io, https://github.com/inteliwear/sidepulse),
released under the MIT License:

  - the LEDS.LED program language, as documented in SidePulse's LEDS_FORMAT.md
  - the agent state model (blocked > needs you > working > done > idle) and the
    20-minute "done" hold
  - the set of Claude Code and Codex hook events, the Codex config.toml hook block
    layout, and the hook-trust registration approach
  - the timing of the built-in animations (roll, kitt, night-rider, tide, attention,
    idle-pulse), reproduced so SidePulse animation files run unchanged

